     <h1>Gibson SG</h1>

     <img src="Images/TED.jpg" width="250" alt="Ted McCarty - President of Gibson and SG Developer">

     <h2>About the SG</h2>
     <p>
         The Gibson SG is one of the most iconic electric guitars ever made. 
         It is known for its light body, fast-playing neck, and sharp, biting tone, making it a favorite among rock and metal guitarists.
     </p>

     <h2>History</h2>
     <p>
         The SG guitar was developed in 1961 by Gibson, under the leadership of company president Ted McCarty. 
         It was originally introduced as a redesign of the Les Paul to create a thinner, lighter alternative with double-cutaway horns. 
         Over the decades, it became Gibson's best-selling model of all time and a true symbol of rock music.
     </p>

     <h2>Common Uses</h2>
     <p>The Gibson SG is especially known for:</p>
     <ul>
         <li>Classic rock and hard rock music</li>
         <li>Heavy metal and aggressive riffs</li>
         <li>Fast, high-register solo playing</li>
         <li>Crunchy, piercing rhythm tones</li>
         <li>Live performances due to its lightweight body</li>
     </ul>

     <h2>Famous Players</h2>
     <p>
         Many legendary guitarists have used the SG, including Angus Young (AC/DC), Tony Iommi (Black Sabbath), and Derek Trucks.
     </p>

